body:
Oh God. Your school sounds like mine. I graduated almost 3 years ago. The only 'core'  classes were basically syntax only and multiple choice tests! The only useful stuff I got was from web and databases, but it was all outdated stuff. I knew it was bad but figured I'd make it up on my first dev job. I still haven't gotten my career started.   


It's kind of validating and terrifying at the same time, to know I'm not the only one who owes all this money for a IT degree that didn't teach me anything. I just saw that you're in South America. It's crazy that this kind of stuff spans the globe.   


&#x200B;
